15 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating study participant selection and analytical workflow for life course adiposity and osteoporosis \(OP\) risk: initial cohort N=488,667, exclusions for missing covariate data and prior OP, resulting in 478,329 participants. Two main analyses\204childhood/adult BMI and birth weight\204involving 357,903 and 207,071 participants, respectively, followed by stratified and sensitivity analyses, then mediation analysis linking adult BMI, proteins, and OP.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 27 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Panel A contains three plots showing hazard ratios for osteoporotic fracture risk: left, a U-shaped curve for birth weight; middle, bar plot of childhood body size categories; right, inverse relationship with adult BMI. Panel B presents mediation diagrams with percentage mediation and confidence intervals from birth weight through body size or adult BMI to osteoporotic fracture, highlighting significant mediation effects by adult BMI and body size.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Forest plot and summary table showing hazard ratios and 95 percent confidence intervals for adiposity measures\204birth weight, childhood body size, adult BMI, and developmental mismatch\204across three models, with reference categories and p-values provided for each comparison.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a volcano plot of proteins with effect sizes on BMI, separated by positive \(red\) and negative \(blue\) associations. Panel B displays a scatter plot of proteins showing log hazard ratios versus negative log FDR, also divided by association direction. Panel C presents a core protein-protein interaction network with nodes labeled by protein names and node size indicating degree. Panel D features a KEGG pathway enrichment bubble chart with pathways on the y-axis, gene ratio on the x-axis, bubble size representing gene count, and color indicating adjusted p-values.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
